Z||000006||loafer87gt||09-13-2001||02:30 AM||||The city of york one I found disturbing. One of my friends just sent me the following email:<P>&gt; &gt; &gt; &gt; Nostradamus Knew<BR> &gt; &gt; &gt; &gt;<BR> &gt; &gt; &gt; &gt; "In the year of the new century and nine months,<BR> &gt; &gt; &gt; &gt; From the sky will come a great King of Terror...<BR> &gt; &gt; &gt; &gt; The sky will burn at forty-five degrees.<BR> &gt; &gt; &gt; &gt; Fire approaches the great new city..."<BR> &gt; &gt; &gt; &gt;<BR> &gt; &gt; &gt; &gt; "In the city of york there will be a great collapse,<BR> &gt; &gt; &gt; &gt; 2 twin brothers torn apart by chaos<BR> &gt; &gt; &gt; &gt; while the fortress falls the great leader will succumb<BR> &gt; &gt; &gt; &gt; third big war will begin when the big city is burning"<BR> &gt; &gt; &gt; &gt;<BR> &gt; &gt; &gt; &gt; - NOSTRADAMUS<BR> &gt; &gt; &gt; &gt;<BR> &gt; &gt; &gt; &gt; He said this will be bigger than the previous two.<BR> &gt; &gt; &gt; &gt;<BR> &gt; &gt; &gt; &gt;<BR> &gt; &gt; &gt; &gt; 2001 is the first year of the new century and<BR> &gt; &gt; &gt; &gt; this is the 9th month.<BR> &gt; &gt; &gt; &gt; New York is located at the 41st degree Latitude.<BR> &gt; &gt; &gt; &gt;||||reg||1
Z||000007||Mach10||09-13-2001||02:58 AM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_bs.gif"><P>Although chilling, I don't really hold much for pophetic drabble. Coincidence? Maybe. Is it a coincidence that none of this drabble makes any sense until you start plugging data AFTER the supposed fact?<P>The quatrain can mean ANYTHING. <BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>At forty-five degrees, the sky will burn,Fire approaches the great new city, Immediately a huge, scattered flame leaps upWhen they want to have verification from the Norman (Century VI, Quatrain 97)<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Lets run some examples:<P>45degC weather. New Delhi burns to the ground, due to fire at some large building or other... Prophecy fulfilled.<P>Smog in any city with the word "new" in it, sun at later afternoon evening casts red-ish glow. (Sky on fire, sun 45* above horizon) and some english dude drops a cig at a gas depository. Whoosh! Prophecy fulfilled.<P>Stupid, hypothetical examples, but all concievable. Large collections of vague data can tell you whatever you'd like to hear. It's like statistics.<P>If Nostradamus KNEW something, why'd he not just come out and say it straight?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000008||Urchin||09-13-2001||03:01 AM||||This is not the one I had initially come across, but it is close.  These are obviously interpretations, not direct quotes.<P>World War III<P>Nostradamus gives two dates for the start of the next World War. Interpreters say this means the rumblings of war will begin in 1994 and a nuclear world war will be under way in 1999.<P>The war on the west will be waged by the third Antichrist, an Arab “from the kingdom of Muhammad” wearing a blue turban will be aligned with Russia.<P>Nostradamus describes the first nuclear attack of WW III as being on a new city located at 45 degrees that is filled with man-made mountains (skyscrapers). According to several interpreters, this is almost a direct reference to New York City.<P>Whether the third Antichrist is Mummar Gaddafy, the son of the Ayatollah or someone yet unknown has not been determined.<P>According to the seer, World War III will last 27 years and little will be left of the world. However, an alliance between the U.S. and Russia will defeat the third Antichrist and oversee a thousand years of peace after the war.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.temple.edu/column/issues/vXIIIn5/classic.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.temple.edu/column/issues/vXIIIn5/classic.htm</A> <p>[This message has been edited by Urchin (edited 09-13-2001).]||||reg||1
